  "Question": "If \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are positive and \\(a\\ne1,\\) \\(b\\ne1,\\) then the value of \\(b^{\\log_b a}\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "dependent upon \\(b\\)",
    "B": "dependent upon \\(a\\)",
    "C": "dependent upon \\(a\\) and \\(b\\)",
    "D": "zero",
    "E": "one"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The conditions \\(a>0\\), \\(b>0\\), and \\(b\\ne1\\) ensure that \\(\\log_b a\\) is defined. By definition, \\(t=\\log_b a\\) means \\(b^t=a\\). Therefore\n\\[\nb^{\\log_b a}=a.\n\\]\nThe value depends only on \\(a\\), so the answer is B.",
